#import "../defs.typ": *


Throughout this chapter, unnamed constants $C$ may change from line to line.
They may depend on fixed problem parameters and may absorb fixed powers of
$a^(-1)$, but they never hide dependence on $n$, $alpha$, $p$, or $q$. Any
dependence on these four variables is displayed explicitly or appears as an
argument of a named quantity. Named constants follow the same convention:
fixed problem factors may be absorbed only when they are not being tracked
explicitly in the surrounding display.
